Z||000004||rigdonhome||08-19-2001||10:42 PM||||I got the 135hp number from another post I put up about 1/4 mile times...  It seemed right because the '88's seem to post slightly slower times.  Maybe it isn't right?  Here's the link to the 1/4 mile post...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012835.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012835.html</A> <P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black<BR>5 speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Cherry!||||reg||11
Z||000005||HummelHund||08-19-2001||11:25 PM||||From what I understand, the 88' Fieros were slower 1/4 mile cars due to the increased weight of the new suspension. They handled light years ahead of the older cars, but traded a bit of quickness for it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||08-19-2001||11:25 PM||||Moist of the auto mags also used the 135hp rating in their tech sections. '88 also has the advantage of neutrally balaned crank and flywheel over previous years.<P>7.5 to 60 is the fastest I've heard, and that was acomplished by MW with a Formula('88).<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
